VPS workspaces in Orca live on a paired Orca server ("Endo VPS Server", orcad over an SSH tunnel), not the desktop runtime. For them, workspace.readContext gives only the repo's display name, an empty branch and no terminals, so the panel found no workspace and never loaded.

The worker now:
- asks each paired server (orca repo list / worktree list --environment, from the local listing's omittedHostSelectors) and matches the repo name;
- reads the trail and findings with this desktop's entire --repo <origin URL> --branch <branch>, from a folder outside any checkout;
- marks repo status, checkpoints and the diff as only readable on the server, since the worker can't run commands there (passphrase-protected SSH key, no ssh-agent; Orca's CLI runs commands there only in terminal tabs);
- shows the server's branch and path in the panel, and a repo that isn't on Entire as a plain message.

Known limit: two worktrees of one repo on a server can't be told apart until readContext carries a path. Verified in Orca on the VPS (endo.chat_backend shows trail #376) and with the harness's new `repo <name>` scenario.
